{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-008-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SessionMergerTests.cs","line":760,"method":"MergeTree_RelativeThreadsCurrentRecordingFormatThroughProductionCallers","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/SessionMerger.cs:100; make the relative boundary measurement refuse the current format (recordingFormatVersion != 0) -> red; passing any other version value stays green because TryGetBodyFixedBoundaryPoint (SessionMerger.cs:1192) never reads the parameter","what_it_asserts":"Merging a tree whose recording carries same-anchor Relative sections with a sub-ms boundary dt reports boundaryDiscontinuityMeters ~30m through MergeTree and emits no boundary-skip log.","why_weak":"rec.RecordingFormatVersion = CurrentRecordingFormatVersion is inert on this path: MergeTree only forwards the value to MeasureRelativeAwareBoundary/TryGetBodyFixedBoundaryPoint, whose body never reads it, so the fixture yields the same 30m for any version value and cannot witness the threading the name claims. The merged recording's own RecordingFormatVersion (copied at SessionMerger.cs:125) is never asserted.","proposed_action":"Rename to name the anchor-local merge path and add Assert.Equal(RecordingStore.CurrentRecordingFormatVersion, merged.RecordingFormatVersion); revisit only if a real per-version gate lands in the measurement path.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
